From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:15:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: shell-drawn password save prompt and
 autofill dropdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan C13. The bridge's views for //chrome's password bubble and Autofill
popup (the hooks of the previous patch), registered when the engine starts
(openarc::InstallBridgeAutofillHost):

- OACPasswordSavePrompt (OACAutofill.h): when the password manager would pop
  up its save / update bubble after a login form submission, the bridge
  builds Chrome's SaveUpdateBubbleController and hands the tab's dialog
  delegate a request with the username and the password length (the
  password stays in the engine). Save (optionally with an edited username),
  Never for this site, Not now / No thanks, or a dismissal go to the bubble
  controller as Chrome's Views bubble sends them. Other bubble states
  (saved confirmation, manage, leak warnings, passkeys) are not shown yet.
- OACAutofillPopup: AutofillPopupView for the shell. Rows (kind, main and
  minor text, label, selectable, acceptable), the field's bounds in the tab
  view's coordinates, text direction and highlighted row; updates while the
  user types go to -tab:didUpdateAutofillPopup:. Keyboard focus stays in the
  page: ↑ / ↓ / Return / Tab / Escape / Shift+Delete are handled in the
  page's key press handler, as the Views popup does; the shell forwards
  hover and clicks. Choosing a row gives the page its focus back.
  Sub-popups are not drawn.

Passwords are stored by //chrome's profile password store, encrypted by
os_crypt with the keychain item named by patch 0014.
